 or restriction of food intake due to one or more of the following: lack of interest in eating or food, sensitivity to sensory characteristics of food (such as taste, texture, smell, or appearance), or concern about aversive consequences of eating (such as choking or vomiting), resulting in persistent failure to meet appropriate nutritional and/or energy needs as manifested by significant weight loss, nutritional deficiency, dependence on enteral feeding or nutritional supplements, or marked interference with psychosocial functioning, and where the eating disturbance is not better explained by lack of available food, cultural or religious practices, another mental disorder, or a concurrent medical condition.\" [PMID:38849953]\n658231: subset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051057\"}\n658232: synonym: \"ARFID\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [DOID:0051057, PMID:38849953]\n658233: synonym: \"selective eating disorder\" EXACT [PMID:38849953]\n658234: xref: DOID:0051057 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\n658235: xref: ICD10CM:F50.82 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\n658236: xref: ICD9:307.59 {source=\"MONDO:relatedTo\"}\n658237: xref: MESH:D000080146 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\n658238: is_a: MONDO:0005451 {source=\"PMID:38849953\"} ! eating disorder\n658239: property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3311-7320\n658240: property_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9408\" xsd:anyURI\n658241: \n658242: [Term]\n658243: id: MONDO:7770003\n\n(Showing lines 658214-658243 of 659067. Use offset=658244 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: MONDO:7770001\nname: equine juvenile spinocerebellar ataxia, FDXR-related, horse\ndef: \"Any spinocerebellar ataxia that occurs in horses due to a variation in the FDXR gene. EJSCA is a degenerative axonopathy characterized by acute onset of ataxia within the first month of life, affecting the pelvic limbs more severely than the thoracic limb and rapidly progressing to inability 